in":"at 17 (printed)","status":"verified","target_quote":"primary aim","line":50,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-6-1-1-cd2564ce","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":28,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"7","text":"ECF No. 68","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-068","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 68","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":51,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-7-1-1-16072c5f","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"7","text":"§ II, supra","n":"1","kind":"internal","target_doc":"DDC-072","target_page":"2","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ II","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":52,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-7-1-1-d61304cd","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"7","text":"Local Civil Rule 7(e)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Local Rules AUG_2025","target_page":"29","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"LCvR 7(e)","status":"verified","target_quote":"A memorandum of points and authorities in support of or in opposition to a motion shall not exceed 45 pages and a reply memorandum shall not exceed 25 pages, without prior approval of the Court. Documents that fail to comply with this provision shall not be filed by the Clerk.","line":53,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-7-1-1-efd2ac16","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":29,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"7","text":"ECF No. 69","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-069","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 69","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":54,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-7-1-1-6eb0b688","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"7","text":"ECF No. 70","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-070","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 70","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":55,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-7-1-1-777e72d0","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"8","text":"Exhibit 1","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-072-01","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF 72-1","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":56,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-8-1-1-54eb0a85","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"8","text":"Standing Order § 7(e)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"2026.03.04 FINAL CIVIL STANDING ORDER (ACR)","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 7(e)","status":"verified","target_quote":"A proposed order should be submitted whenever a party requests relief from the Court, including for matters as routine as proposing a new date for a joint status report (with an exception for FOIA cases, as noted above, supra Section 5.d). Proposed orders should be filed on the docket as a PDF attachment to the corresponding motion, and counsel must also submit proposed orders to the Court by emailing a Microsoft Word version of the draft to reyes_proposedorders@dcd.uscourts.gov. The subject line of the email must include (1) the case name; (2) the case number; (3) the docket number of the corresponding motion; and (4) the title of the order that is proposed as indicated on the Notice of Electronic Filing. Counsel must serve a copy of a proposed order on all other parties by copying them on the email to the Court. Unless the Court directs otherwise, a party must file a motion asking the Court to enter the proposed order. Submitting a draft to the Court's proposed order inbox is not a substitute for a motion. The Court will consider proposed orders when ruling on motions, but will modify (or disregard altogether) such proposed orders as it deems appropriate, even if all parties agree on the proposed order. Proposed orders (such as stipulated protective orders) require Court approval before they are in effect.","line":57,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-8-1-1-1fb5ec2b","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"8","text":"ECF Nos. 69, 70","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-069","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 69","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":58,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-8-1-1-67658879","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"8","text":"ECF Nos. 69, 70","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-070","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 70","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":59,"k":2,"unit_id":"DDC-072-8-1-2-67658879","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-072","src_page":"9","text":"ECF Nos. 69, 70","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-069","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"ECF No. 69","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":60,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-072-9-1-1-67658879","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":9,"targ